message:
{{#is_alert}}The fleet's average cost per model call over the last 4h is over $0.05 — 3x the ~$0.017/call the fleet ran at over the week of 2026-08-27 → 09-03. Something changed the price, not the volume.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}Average cost per model call over the last 4h is over $0.035 — 2x the weekly baseline; worth a look at what ran.{{/is_warning}}

This is the price signal the daily spend guardrail cannot see: a runaway loop, a broken prompt-cache prefix (RC1-350 — pr-review-agent uncached is ~$0.06/call vs ~$0.015 cached), a model swap, or prompt growth all raise cost per call; a busy shipping day does not.

Triage on the [fleet dashboard](https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/bwm-uny-qqs):
- **Prompt caching row**: pr-review-agent cache hit % should sit near 80% during a review; near 0% means the shared prefix broke.
- **Cost by model**: a sonnet subject suddenly on opus shows here first.
- **Cost by ml_app**: the kpi-agent's opus define/instrument/narrate calls are legitimately ~$0.08–0.12 each — a handful in one window can reach the warn line; that is the one known benign trigger.

Query: cost / clamp_min(calls, 10) / 1e9 — the denominator floors at 10 calls so one expensive call cannot trip it on its own. Threshold set from the trailing-7d mean on 2026-09-03 (RC1-377); re-derive it when the fleet's model mix changes.

